course: dictionary
lesson: 6901
title: Owls
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An owl is a bird with a big round face, large forward-facing eyes and a hooked beak. Most owls hunt at night, catching small animals such as mice and voles. «Owls, foxes, cats, weasels, snakes and hawks all hunt mice.» Owls are one of many hunters that eat mice.
explain: Owls are built for night hunting. «Owl wing feathers have comb-like front edges, soft fringes and a velvety surface that muffle the sound of flying.» Muffle means make quieter, so an owl can creep up on its prey without being heard.
explain: Some owl facts in stories are exaggerated. «Some tales are nearly true, like the owl that turns its head all the way round; it turns about three-quarters of the way, and that is amazing enough.» Good readers check a claim against what they know.
explain: Calling a person a «night owl» is a figure of speech. It means someone who likes to stay up late, not someone who is really a bird. The rest of the sentence shows you which meaning is used.
fact: An owl is a bird of prey, and most owls are nocturnal, meaning they are active at night.
fact: «A great grey owl can plunge through deep snow to grab a vole it has only heard.»
fact: Owls have very good hearing and can turn their heads a long way round.
fact: Owls swallow their prey whole and later cough up pellets of fur and bones.
fact: «Barn owl», «tawny owl», «snowy owl» and «owl pellet» are all words about owls.
exercise: What kind of animal is an owl? | A fish that swims in deep water | A snake that lives in trees | *A bird with a big round face and a hooked beak | A small furry animal that hunts by day
exercise: «A family of barn owls can eat over a thousand mice and voles in a year.» What does this tell us? | Owls only eat fish | *Owls are very good hunters of small animals | Owls never eat mice | Owls sleep for a whole year
exercise: Find and copy the word from the feathers sentence that means make quieter. | comb | velvety | *muffle | fringes
test: Which phrase means someone who likes to stay up late? | *Night owl | Snowy owl | Barn owl | Tawny owl
test: In stories, what does the wise old owl usually stand for? | Sleep | Anger | *Wisdom | Speed
exam: How far does a real owl turn its head, according to the story sentence? | Exactly all the way round | Not at all | About a quarter of the way round | *About three-quarters of the way round
